**How to implement.** `MainWorkbenchTests` composes its fresh stores the way the App does (`MainWorkbenchTests.fs:68-85`), so they come from the shipped catalogue too (.spec-md §3.4, §3.5). `freshStores ()` answers `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` (step 41) in place of the two self-seeding stores. `mainWith` takes that bundle and calls `initMainWith (liveLibrary stores.libraryEntries stores.samples (SourceProxy.createInMemory ())) (Experiments.createInMemoryExperiments ()) stores.materials stores.samples stores.categories`, the composition `DefaultStores.create` performs (step 42). The create-picker fact (`:143-146`) reads the bundle's `materials` and `categories` in place of building a category store. The two helpers' docs say they compose from the Built-in catalogue as the App does, and the `Lifecycle`, `MaterialStore` and `SampleStore` opens go if nothing else needs them. Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, and `sampleBandsState collapses a period group to x-N bands (the Details-bay shape)` keeps reading `SeedSamples.multilayerQw`.

**Acceptance.** After the re-point, `MainWorkbenchTests.fs` MUST NOT call `MaterialProxy.createInMemory`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory`, `CategoryProxy.createInMemory` or `Library.createInMemory`; ui-tests (MainWorkbenchTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass with their counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.
